36 days, 4hrs, 4min, and I had to earn every second! My main question though is, "Where's Sasquatch? I know he's out here somewhere..." Seriously though, this has been a joy to play thus far as a survival hobbiest. You will panic at some point, and you will probably die at some point. One story comes to mind;
I just killed a bear, and got greedy. I decided 2 harvest everything...baaaaad move. I came out of the harvest screen to pitch black, in the middle of a blizzard, completely overencumbered. The house was just a short distance away, but I couldn't find it for the life of me. I dropped as much as I 'thought' I could spare(being a hoarder by nature), then wandered blindly, for a few paces, hoping the house would be illuminated by my quickly expiring storm lantern. No go. I ran out of fuel. I had 4 flares. I made a quick fire with the bit of reclaimed wood I had left just to warm up. But it wasn't going to last. I had to do something! Try and find some firewood, or keep looking for the house...exhausted, freezing, damn near starving, I lit a flare. Still wandering, trying to keep my fire in sight, basically blind, and then the flare left me in howling, cold, darkness. It was fight or flight time. I dropped everything else except my knife, hatchet, gun, and my last 3 flares. Lit another one. Just before it went out, my prayers were answered as a silhouette slowly revealed itself; "The car!! That means the house is right over..." I took a hard right, and after a few more paces, the beautiful farm homestead came into view. I was saved!
I survived that night. Somehow. But that is just one of the many expieriences you may have if you play this game. My heart had dropped into my stomach, and I was terrified in real life. And not a zombie in sight lol! You have to be smart, you have to be focused, and you have to plan every move the second you step out of that cozy little house, hut, or radio tower into the wilderness. Or get really, really, lucky! Great game, and loving it so far!
